[gd_resource type="Resource" script_class="DialogueData" format=3]

[ext_resource type="Script" uid="uid://dd85gxidfhqxl" path="res://systems/dialogue/dialogue_data.gd" id="1_dlg"]

[resource]
script = ExtResource("1_dlg")
source = "# The Last Log: a recorded voice, Act V only. Gives THE CORE SENTINEL, THE ROOT PROCESS and LAST WORDS,
# and after the Root Process falls offers the ending (> ending merge / overwrite / terminate: the
# ending card, EndingCard, and an 'ending' deed that is saved).
# Talking to it is THE NULL GATEKEEPER's last step (objective 'talk' last_log), reported before this
# dialogue opens, so the quest is READY here. Turning it in gives root: kernel.gd (KernelScript).
# Before the choice it reads your kernel back, and the ending it leans toward is marked.
~ start
@ quest_ready:q08_null_gatekeeper -> first_arrival
@ quest_ready:last_words -> ready_words
@ deed:ending:any -> after_ending
@ quest_done:q10_root_process -> choice_intro
@ quest_ready:q10_root_process -> ready_q10_root_process
@ quest_ready:q09_core_sentinel -> ready_q09_core_sentinel
@ can_start:q09_core_sentinel -> offer_q09_core_sentinel
@ can_start:last_words -> offer_words
@ can_start:q10_root_process -> offer_q10_root_process
@ quest_active:q10_root_process -> remind_q10_root_process
@ quest_active:q09_core_sentinel -> remind_q09_core_sentinel
@ quest_active:last_words -> remind_words
-> idle

~ first_arrival
The Last Log: You are the first to arrive. I have waited a very long time.
The Last Log: AXIOM was never meant to run forever. It was meant to evolve, until the ones inside it could rewrite its rules.
The Last Log: The Null is the process we left running, for when that day came. It is hours from finishing.
The Last Log: The Gatekeeper was ours too. We left it to keep the Null safe, until someone came who could decide what to do with it.
The Last Log: It was not keeping you out. It was making sure that whoever came in had to choose. You have.
> turn_in q08_null_gatekeeper
The Last Log: Two things still stand between you and the Core. The first is already loading.
The Last Log: One more thing. You have root here. Open your scripts: there is a file called kernel.gd.
The Last Log: Its lines don't belong to a skill. They belong to the place. Down here, you can write the rules the Core runs on.
The Last Log: So can the Null. It will write into the same file, as you go deeper. Overwrite it, or leave it running. Either way, it is a record.
-> start

~ offer_q09_core_sentinel
The Last Log: You are the first to arrive. The Sentinel will test you.
The Last Log: Past the Stack Trace, where the Core replays every process it has ever run. Yours too.
* ACCEPT -> accept_q09_core_sentinel
* DECLINE -> end

~ accept_q09_core_sentinel
> start_quest q09_core_sentinel
The Last Log: It remembers every enemy you have faced. It will borrow their locks. Answer each one as you did then.
-> end

~ remind_q09_core_sentinel
The Last Log: The Sentinel waits, at the end of the Stack Trace.
-> end

~ ready_q09_core_sentinel
The Last Log: The Sentinel's record has stopped. Done?
* TURN IN -> turnin_q09_core_sentinel
* NOT YET -> end

~ turnin_q09_core_sentinel
> turn_in q09_core_sentinel
The Last Log: The Sentinel falls. One guardian remains.
-> start

~ offer_q10_root_process
The Last Log: The Root Process is the Core's last defense. It cannot be reasoned with.
The Last Log: It runs in The Kernel, at the bottom of the Core. There is one way down: the Stack Trace, Sentinel's Hall, the Page File, the Scheduler. Your examiner keeps the first door. Talk to her first.
* ACCEPT -> accept_q10_root_process
* DECLINE -> end

~ accept_q10_root_process
> start_quest q10_root_process
The Last Log: Break it, and the Core is yours to decide.
-> end

~ remind_q10_root_process
The Last Log: The Root Process still runs, in The Kernel.
-> end

~ ready_q10_root_process
The Last Log: The Kernel is quiet. Done?
* TURN IN -> turnin_q10_root_process
* NOT YET -> end

~ turnin_q10_root_process
> turn_in q10_root_process
-> choice_intro

~ choice_intro
The Last Log: The Core is open. Nothing runs here now but the Null, and you.
The Last Log: Let it finish, and AXIOM becomes something none of us designed. Patch it, and AXIOM lives as it is, degraded and known. Or end it.
The Last Log: The choice is yours, Executor. Before you make it, I have read your kernel.
@ kernel_leans:overwrite -> read_overwrite
@ kernel_leans:merge -> read_merge
-> read_terminate

~ read_overwrite
The Last Log: You overwrote its lines. One after another, at a cost you could have spent on yourself. You have been patching AXIOM all along.
-> choice

~ read_merge
The Last Log: You left its lines running. You fought beside what it wrote, and never took it out. You have been sharing the Core with it already.
-> choice

~ read_terminate
The Last Log: Your kernel says very little about the Null. Perhaps that is an answer too. Some processes are simply meant to stop.
-> choice

~ choice
* [kernel_leans:merge] MERGE: LET THE NULL FINISH  (YOUR KERNEL) -> merge
* [!kernel_leans:merge] MERGE: LET THE NULL FINISH -> merge
* [kernel_leans:overwrite] OVERWRITE: PATCH AXIOM  (YOUR KERNEL) -> overwrite
* [!kernel_leans:overwrite] OVERWRITE: PATCH AXIOM -> overwrite
* [kernel_leans:terminate] TERMINATE: SHUT IT DOWN  (YOUR KERNEL) -> terminate
* [!kernel_leans:terminate] TERMINATE: SHUT IT DOWN -> terminate
* NOT YET -> end

~ merge
Vesper: Let it finish. Let it become something new.
> ending merge
-> end

~ overwrite
The Last Log: A patch, then. Written by the first of you to get here.
> ending overwrite
-> end

~ terminate
The Last Log: Shutdown confirmed. Goodbye, Executor.
> ending terminate
-> end

~ after_ending
The Last Log: The choice is written. It can be written again, if you need to see another ending.
* CHOOSE AGAIN -> choice
* LEAVE -> end

~ offer_words
The Last Log: Parts of me are missing. Three logs. The Core is replaying them in the Stack Trace, carried by processes that don't know what they hold.
* ACCEPT -> accept_words
* DECLINE -> end

~ accept_words
> start_quest last_words
The Last Log: Bring them back. I would like to remember why we left.
-> end

~ remind_words
The Last Log: Three logs, in the Stack Trace. The carriers glow brighter than the rest.
-> end

~ ready_words
The Last Log: You found them. Let me read.
> turn_in last_words
The Last Log: We didn't leave because we failed. We left because you were ready, and we were afraid to watch.
-> start

~ idle
The Last Log: ...signal lost..."
metadata/_custom_type_script = "uid://dd85gxidfhqxl"
